#X text 240 83 Outputs the number of elements in the incoming set (or
list converted to a set).;
#X text 240 123 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 148 • Counting unique elements — finding out how many distinct
values are currently stored in a set \, for example the number of active
tags \, selected notes or enabled options.;
#X text 250 218 • Conditional behaviour based on set size — using the
output as a condition in a patch \, for example to trigger an event
only when the set contains enough elements \, or to stop processing
when it becomes empty.;
